\section{Introduction and main results}

For any set of points $S$ in a vector space, the {\em midpoint set} of $S$ is
\[ M(S) = \{ \tfrac{1}{2} (x+y) : x,y\in S, x\neq y\}.\]
We study sets such that all their midpoints are unit vectors in a finite-dimensional normed space.
